Declare the vendor charger-manager config the published tree forgot

The vendor defconfig carries CONFIG_IFLYTEK_CHARGER_MANAGER=y but the
published Kernel_OpenSource tree never declared that symbol, so
olddefconfig drops it silently. Meanwhile CONFIG_CHARGER_SC2703=y still
builds sc2703-charger.o, which calls cm_notify_event() -- a symbol that
only exists when charger-manager.c is compiled in. The link then dies at
vmlinux with:

    undefined reference to `cm_notify_event'

The driver source is present in the tree, so this is purely a missing
Kconfig declaration. Add an alias that selects CHARGER_MANAGER, which is
what the vendor symbol effectively meant.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
@@
+config IFLYTEK_CHARGER_MANAGER
+	bool "Vendor charger manager alias (declared by vendor config)"
+	depends on REGULATOR
+	select CHARGER_MANAGER
+	help
+	  The vendor defconfig sets CONFIG_IFLYTEK_CHARGER_MANAGER=y, but the
+	  published tree never declared it, so olddefconfig silently dropped it
+	  and drivers referencing cm_notify_event() failed to link. This alias
+	  simply selects CHARGER_MANAGER.
+
 config CHARGER_MANAGER
 	bool "Battery charger manager for multiple chargers"
 	depends on REGULATOR
